          <groundspeak:finder id="1685537">nosweat6060</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP330 NGP [FOUND]

Cap #3 for the morning. So far, so good. Thanks to everyone involved in setting up and maintaining this activity. I love it! It is a definite addition to the overall geocaching experience.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684635904">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="6304346">sapien</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP330 NGP

N 50° 59.157 W 114° 07.357&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I struggled with this one.  My GZ was about 3m away from where I actually found the cap.  In fact, after not finding it initially, I actually went back to the car to do a little more research.  After studying some of the previous logs, I came back and found the cap right away.  As I was taking my waypoint average, I noticed a couple walking towards me.  It turns out to be geoCurious2 who surprise surprise just happens to be for the same reason.  What a surprise! :-)  I love meeting other cachers out on the hunt.  We had a great conversation here and as we searched for the next cap and a cache together.  TFTBC.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684189973">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7573673">geoCurious2</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP330 - NGP&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We decided to geocache on the north side of the Glenmore Reservoir today and pick up 4 Brass Caps along the way.  We had the pleasure of meeting up with Sapiens who, like us, was trying to pick up as many Brass Caps as possible in last couple of days.  (that's his Garmin in the photo!)&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683867422">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="2034047">Cachin8r</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP330 NGP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sixth of 12 today, #863. This one was definitely the trickiest find of all the caps we did today. I had to do a double-take on the hint provided because it didn't match the surroundings at all. Looked for several minutes in probably the wrong areas. We went back to the vehicle to look at past photos, and to get the third (reserve) set of eyes. Upon returning we were lucky and walked right up to it. This one really blended in. Thanks for another cap!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;-Cachin&lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_8ball.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;r&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683464566">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="4883787">Kottbullar</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP330 NGP&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This cache is BG, so as I was trying to get a picture, I needed to be on my hands and knees. A couple of muggles walked by and gave me a good stare as I though about Praying to the Brass Cap God and had a giggle!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
